# list[at] = a / b: the quotient may be NaN, and whatever bits the division gave it go into the bytes. The double is stored as it is.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="put" role=Source
# CHECK: Double b@[[quotient]] = Div(b@{{*}}, b@{{*}}, ControlDependent, {{*}}:Div)
# CHECK: Store(b@[[quotient]], b@{{*}}, ControlDependent|Writes:TypedArrayElements, {{*}}:PutTypedArrayElement)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# Nothing compares the quotient with itself, looks at its bits or chooses another NaN.
# NONE-LABEL: name="put" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: Equal(
# NONE-NOT: BitwiseCast
# NONE-NOT: Select(
# NONE-NOT: Double b@{{*}} = Phi(
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# The patchpoint keeps the array alive and emits nothing.
# X64: instructions: 9, patchpoints: 1
# ARM64: instructions: 10, patchpoints: 1
